@node gpui-d3rs User Guide
@section User Guide

Users see @code{gpui-d3rs} as the rendering layer behind every chart
in the desktop player:

@itemize @bullet
@item Line / scatter plots for measurements.
@item Iso-line and contour plots for predicted-in-room response and
  directivity.
@item Radar, polar, 3D contour for advanced views.
@end itemize

There is no user-facing configuration; chart appearance follows the
active theme (@ref{gpui-themes Manual}).

@node gpui-d3rs Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

@subheading Primitives

@table @code
@item Scales
@code{LinearScale}, @code{LogScale}, with automatic tick generation.
@item Shapes
Lines, bars, areas, arcs, pies, scatter.
@item Colours
RGB/HSL, interpolation, categorical schemes.
@item Geographic projections
Mercator, orthographic.
@item Spatial
QuadTree, Delaunay (via @ref{math-delaunay Manual}), Voronoi.
@item Animation
Transitions, easing functions, timers.
@end table

@subheading Builder-style API

D3's functional chaining is replaced by Rust builders:

@example
let chart = LineChart::new()
    .data(&points)
    .x_scale(LinearScale::new(0.0, 20_000.0))
    .y_scale(LinearScale::new(-30.0, 10.0))
    .stroke(theme.accent);
@end example

@subheading Showcases

Two demo binaries ship with the crate; see the README and
@file{examples/}.

@subheading Testing

@example
cargo test -p gpui-d3rs
@end example
